After several days of flashing smileys on Clearblue Advanced Digital, I finally got a solid smiley (peak fertility) today on</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">31 minutes ago </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-78751826" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a6720413/getting_pregnant_trying_to_conceive">Getting Pregnant - Trying to Conceive </a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a78751826/question">Question?</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-nkvp61" size="20" aria-hidden="true">c</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By CaityCatGirl </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">I ovulated on the 9th according to my period app. My period is one day late, but I am getting negative tests?

Facts:
My period is never late
We tried(had sex) the 7th and 9th.
I had a lot of cramping on Sunday evening, in the same areas I had with my daughter before I found out.
I took a pregnancy </div><div class="timestamp finePrint">6 hours ago </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-78751767" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/groups/a6720413/getting_pregnant_trying_to_conceive">Getting Pregnant - Trying to Conceive </a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/post/a78751767/need-help">Need help</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-a7usph" size="20" aria-hidden="true">a</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By alwaysalibra </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">I have been ttc since last month. unfortunately i got my cycle this month. we are trying again and i started taking mucinex during my fertile window and during ovulation. i am 10 dpo. if anybody who has taken mucinex, when did you get prego symptoms. </div><div class="timestamp finePrint">14 hours ago </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-