akes him 40 minutes to an hour to fall asleep. It's really not ideal, but the alternative is him screaming for an hour. But now we've created this expectation of not going to bed alone. And it's turned into mi","url":"/post/a78751440/cosleeping-and-separation-anxiety","isSensitive":null,"createDate":"2026-10-22T21:39:51.000Z","updateDate":"2026-10-22T21:39:51.000Z","lastActivityDate":"2026-10-23T11:04:35.000Z","cmntCount":2,"images":[],"giphies":[],"user":{"globalUserId":"G8Qg0PKtLxUf7BaJ","screenName":"Jul1a6","imageUrl":null,"__typename":"UserPublic"},"updateUser":{"globalUserId":"G8Qg0PKtLxUf7BaJ","screenName":"Jul1a6","imageUrl":null,"__typename":"UserPublic"},"group":{"globalUserId":"AZs6W8TXI5YGkZZe","id":"199215","title":"Teaching Your Baby and Toddler To Sleep","url":"/groups/a199215/teaching_your_baby_and_toddler_to_sleep","__typename":"Group"},"lastActivityUser":{"screenName":"Jul1a6","__typename":"UserPublic"},"reactions":{"types":[],"count":0,"__typename":"ReactionSummary"},"poll":null,"__typename":"Post"},{"id":"78751412","globalUserId":"hHd71uSGLYbEKE9k","title":"FTM Sleep Training","bodySnippet":"This message is specifically for ftms who are debating whether sleep training is the right decision for their child.\n\nAs an ftm who ended up co-sleeping with my baby because he didn’t like the bassinet or crib for the past 8 weeks, I came to the realization that it was no longer healthy for me to co","url":"/post/a78751412/ftm-sleep-training","isSensitive":null,"createDate":"2026-10-22T20:59:23.000Z","updateDate":"2026-10-22T20:59:23.000Z","lastActivityDate":"2026-10-23T13:51:53.000Z","cmntCount":10,"images":[],"giphies":[],"user":{"globalUserId":"hHd71uSGLYbEKE9k","screenName":"Ftmtam24","imageUrl":null,"__typename":"UserPublic"},"updateUser":{"globalUserId":"hHd71uSGLYbEKE9k","screenName":"Ftmtam24","imageUrl":null,"__typename":"UserPublic"},"group":{"globalUserId":"DS1i6TjNxQtWjOi2","id":"125","title":"Babies","url":"/groups/a125/babies","__typename":"Group"},"lastActivityUser":{"screenName":"RaisingWarriors247","__typename":"UserPublic"},"reactions":{"types":["hug"],"count":7,"__typename":"ReactionSummary"},"poll":null,"__typename":"Post"},{"id":"78750944","globalUserId":"YiPoDK96hwWXyCs2","title":"Newborn ","bodySnippet":"Does anyone else have a hard time waking their newborn up too eat??. ","url":"/post/a78750944/newborn","isSensitive":null,"createDate":"2026-10-21T12:53:43.000Z","updateDate":"2026-10-21T12:53:43.000Z","lastActivityDate":"2026-10-22T13:05:48.000Z","cmntCount":6,"images":[],"giphies":[],"user":{"globalUserId":"YiPoDK96hwWXyCs2","screenName":"BiancaMaria1992","imageUrl":"https://static.babycenter.com/user/YiPoDK96hwWXyCs2/us-299db592-9255-4221-97dc-7f1cb1a67f3f","__typename":"UserPublic"},"updateUser":{"globalUserId":"YiPoDK96hwWXyCs2","screenName":"BiancaMaria1992","imageUrl":"https://static.babycenter.com/user/YiPoDK96hwWXyCs2/us-299db592-9255-4221-97dc-7f1cb1a67f3f","__typename":"UserPublic"},"group":{"globalUserId":"DS1i6TjNxQtWjOi2","id":"125","title":"Babies","url":"/groups/a125/babies","__typename":"Group"},"lastActivityUser":{"screenName":"BooneMomma2","__typename":"UserPublic"},"reactions":{"types":["hug"],"count":2,"__typename":"ReactionSummary"},"poll":null,"__typename":"Post"},{"id":"78750931","globalUserId":"t0DlEj5RaL7cuQZu","title":"Sleep training - gradual withdrawal ","bodySnippet":"LO’s age: 6months \nComplete sleep schedule :\n7am wake up \n9am - nap 1 - 1.5 hr \n12:30 - nap 2 - 1hr \n3:30pm - nap 3 1.5hr \n6:30 bath \n7:30 book, feed  and down for bed \n\nSleep environment : crib in our room , no pacifier.\n\n\nUp until 3/4 days ago I was feeding her to sleep I stopped this and started ","url":"/post/a78750931/sleep-training-gradual-withdrawal","isSensitive":null,"createDate":"2026-10-21T11:15:56.000Z","updateDate":"2026-10-21T11:15:56.000Z","lastActivityDate":"2026-10-22T19:44:19.000Z","cmntCount":1,"images":[],"giphies":[],"user":{"globalUserId":"t0DlEj5RaL7cuQZu","screenName":"Mukaziwapaafrica13","imageUrl":"https://static.babycenter.com/user/t0DlEj5RaL7cuQZu/2410617e-3816-4e08-8bdc-7068bf07fa33","__typename":"UserPublic"},"updateUser":{"globalUserId":"t0DlEj5RaL7cuQZu","screenName":"Mukaziwapaafrica13","imageUrl":"https://static.babycenter.com/user/t0DlEj5RaL7cuQZu/2410617e-3816-4e08-8bdc-7068bf07fa33","__typename":"UserPublic"},"group":{"globalUserId":"AZs6W8TXI5YGkZZe","id":"199215","title":"Teaching Your Baby and Toddler To Sleep","url":"/groups/a199215/teaching_your_baby_and_toddler_to_sleep","__typename":"Group"},"lastActivityUser":{"screenName":"AllisonRebeccah","__typename":"UserPublic"},"reactions":{"types":[],"count":0,"__typename":"ReactionSummary"},"poll":null,"__typename":"Post"},{"id":"78750844","globalUserId":"L6TF46VE15N94Vim","title":"Formula","bodySnippet":"FTM here. I was exclusively breastfeeding but my milk isn’t enough for baby anymore. The pediatrician recommended starting formula to add in with my breast milk. Do I need to boil water to mix with the formula or is bottled water okay to use? I have never used formula before so I’m not sure. My baby","url":"/post/a78750844/formula","isSensitive":null,"createDate":"2026-10-20T21:33:32.000Z","updateDate":"2026-10-20T21:33:32.000Z","lastActivityDate":"2026-10-21T11:06:28.000Z","cmntCount":8,"images":[],"giphies":[],"user":{"globalUserId":"L6TF46VE15N94Vim","screenName":"0Kim0","imageUrl":null,"__typename":"UserPublic"},"updateUser":{"globalUserId":"L6TF46VE15N94Vim","screenName":"0Kim0","imageUrl":null,"__typename":"UserPublic"},"group":{"globalUserId":"DS1i6TjNxQtWjOi2","id":"125","title":"Babies","url":"/groups/a125/babies","__typename":"Group"},"lastActivityUser":{"screenName":"HighEmpress","__typename":"UserPublic"},"reactions":{"types":[],"count":0,"__typename":"ReactionSummary"},"poll":null,"__typename":"Post"},{"id":"78750778","globalUserId":"9Blf2RwWwuCymbDZ","title":"Teething? ","bodySnippet":"This is my second and he seems to be super irritated and constantl